<Layout
  title="Delete your Horizon account"
  description="How to delete your Horizon account and kingdom, what is deleted, what is kept and how long backups last."
  crumbs={[['Wiki', ''], ['Delete your account', 'delete-account/']]}
>
  <h1>Delete your Horizon account</h1>
  <p class="lede">Horizon: Tides of War, by Nirah Digital (on Google Play and the App Store). You can delete your account and everything kept for it at any time.</p>

  <h2>In the game</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Horizon and tap <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
    <li>Open the <strong>Account</strong> tab and tap <strong>Clear all data</strong>.</li>
    <li>Confirm. Your account is deleted at once, on our servers and on the phone.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>If you can't open the game</h2>
  <p>
    Email us at <a href="mailto:nirah@nirah.co?subject=Delete%20my%20Horizon%20account">nirah@nirah.co</a> (or write through
    <a href="https://nirah.co/legal/support">Nirah Digital support</a>) with the subject <strong>“Delete my Horizon account”</strong>, and include your
    lord code (shown on your profile) or the Google or Apple account you linked. We delete the account within 30 days and tell you when it is done.
  </p>

  <h2>What is deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your kingdom (buildings, goods, gems, army, progress) and its copy on our servers.</li>
    <li>Your public card (name, crest, trophies, emblems), your mail and raid reports, your letters to the team, your chat block list and your push-notification token.</li>
    <li>Your sign-in account, including a linked Google or Apple account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Chat messages you already sent stay in the realm chat, but <strong>anonymised</strong>: your lord name is replaced with “Former lord”, the link to
      your account is removed, the Keep level, trophies and emblem beside the name go, and @mentions of your name are cut from them. Moderation copies and
      reports about those messages, and reports you made, are anonymised the same way.
    </li>
    <li>Records of purchases (product, date, store receipt), as the law and the app stores require, and so a purchase is never paid out twice.</li>
    <li>Who invited whom, so invite rewards can't be claimed twice.</li>
    <li>Anonymous daily totals for the whole game (for example how many raids were fought), which say nothing about you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Backups</h2>
  <p>
    Our server keeps encrypted backups for disaster recovery. Deleted data disappears from them as they expire: within <strong>8 weeks</strong> of the
    deletion at the latest. Backups are used only to restore the game after a failure.
  </p>

  <p class="small muted">See also the <a href="https://nirah.co/legal/privacy#horizon">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</Layout>
